 * @section power_stage_configuration Configuration at CELL -> Power Stage
 * 
 * This section describes the PWM control and fault signals for the power stage configuration.
 * 
 * - **PWM Control**:
 *     - `PWMAH_OI1`: PWM leg A, upper switch - leftmost RX
 *     - `PWMAL_OI2`: PWM leg A, lower switch - second from the left RX
 *     - `PWMBH_OI3`: PWM leg B, upper switch - second from the right RX
 *     - `PWMBL_OI4`: PWM leg B, lower switch - rightmost RX
 * 
 * - **Fault Signals**:
 *     - **OFault1, 2, 3**: Fault signals merged next to `PWMBL_OI4` (rightmost).
 *     - Fault Rx is also included in the merged fault signal from other cells or system parts.
 *     - **InFault1, 2**: Fault input from other parts of the system.
 * 
 * - **Enable PWM**:
 *     - `EN_OI5`: Enable PWM, next to `OFault3`.
 * 
 * - **Isolation Switch**:
 *     - `IN_ISW`: Isolation switch, isolates the winding, located next to `EN_OI5`.
 *
 * @section adc_sensor_mapping ADC and Sensor Mapping for Cells
 * 
 * This section provides details on the connections (CONN1-4) for each cell, the current and voltage sensor mapping, 
 * and the related ADC inputs. It also describes the filtering process and sampling rates.
 * 
 * - **Signal Filtering**: The signal is filtered using LEM + OpAmp + anti-aliasing filters, where the OpAmp introduces a significant delay of 2 microseconds.
 * - **ADC Sampling Rate**: The maximum sample rate of the ADC is 1.1 MSamples/second. Since ADCA has 5 active channels, the effective sample rate is reduced to 220 kSamples/second per channel.
 * 
 * <table>
 * <tr><th>Cell</th><th>Connector</th><th>Sensor</th><th>Pin</th><th>ADC Input</th></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 1</td><td>CONN1</td><td>Current sensor</td><td>7</td><td>ADCIn1 : ADCCIN_C4</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 1</td><td>CONN1</td><td>Voltage sensor</td><td>8</td><td>ADCIn2 : ADCCIN_C3</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 2</td><td>CONN2</td><td>Current sensor</td><td>7</td><td>ADCIn3 : ADCCIN_C2</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 2</td><td>CONN2</td><td>Voltage sensor</td><td>8</td><td>ADCIn4 : ADCCIN_A5</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 3</td><td>CONN3</td><td>Current sensor</td><td>7</td><td>ADCIn5 : ADCCIN_A4</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 3</td><td>CONN3</td><td>Voltage sensor</td><td>8</td><td>ADCIn6 : ADCCIN_A3</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 4</td><td>CONN4</td><td>Current sensor</td><td>7</td><td>ADCIn7 : ADCCIN_A2</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Cell 4</td><td>CONN4</td><td>Voltage sensor</td><td>8</td><td>ADCIn8 : ADCCIN_A1</td></tr>
 * </table> 
